      w: `The mirror used for seeing: reflection taken as information about your own shape, not as a race. Done, it looks like gratitude at a distance: the other side studied for what it reveals, then left in peace. Its answer is the Echo: what faces you in space will return in time; a reflection read honestly now saves years of hearing it later.`,
      a: `Living in the mirror: residence taken up in the comparison, the second image consulted before every act. The carry is the self deferred: a life spent synchronised to a reflection never quite becomes its own original.`,
      q: `What is the mirror showing that you keep reading as competition?`,
